# In Python, # starts a comment. In C, # starts a preprocessor directive.
```

Wait, Python doesn't have `/* */` comments. So `/* comment */` in Python would be a syntax error.

Let me think differently. I can use:
1. Python's `#` comments which are also valid in C (as preprocessor directives or just as lines starting with #)
2. String literals that both languages understand

A common trick:
```c
